      \field{annotation}{Sections read: Ch. 69 sec. 1 (approved 2 February 1875), "township" in any statute passed before 3 November 1874 is to be read as the magisterial districts the amendment directs; ch. 76 sec. 1 (approved 5 February 1875), the townships as they existed "on the third day of November, eighteen hundred and seventy-four, (the date of the ratification of amendment to the constitution respecting county organization)" are "hereby declared to be, the magisterial districts", keeping their boundaries, names and voting places; ch. 158 sec. 4 (approved 8 March 1875), in each magisterial district the qualified voters choose one supervisor, one constable, three justices and one overseer of the poor. Ch. 76 is the act that carried out the constitutional amendment on county organization ratified 3 November 1874; it renames the unit and leaves the officers alone. The amendment itself is not in this volume; it is cited separately as \cite{vaacts1873amendment}. Ch. 158 is titled "An act to provide for the Election and Qualification of County Officers" and is the general law under which supervisors were elected from 1875; sec. 4 names the electorate ("the qualified voters of the same"), fixes the term at two years, and states no residence qualification for any of the four district officers it creates. The copy held is a seven-page extract of the Internet Archive scan of the Google-digitized volume: the title page and printed pages 52, 56-58, 133 and 134. The scan carries no text layer, so chapter numbers and approval dates were read off the page images. Nothing else in the volume has been read. Two sessions cut excerpts on 26 September 2026 and they are combined here. Filed in Drive as "legal/state statutes/Commonwealth of Virginia 1875 - Acts and Joint Resolutions, Session of 1874-75 (ch. 69, 76 and 158 excerpt).pdf"}
