      \field{annotation}{Ch. 443, Acts of the General Assembly of Virginia, session of 1952, printed p. 732, approved 1 April 1952 [S 431]. The non-interference bar, and the one structural change of the 1952 session enacted outright rather than offered to the voters. The act is titled as "relating to interference by members of county boards in appointments and removals of certain personnel". New sec. 15-350.1 in full: "Except as to persons appointed by it, neither the county board nor any of its members shall direct or request the appointment of any person to or his removal from any office or employment by the county or in any way take part in the appointment of or removal of officers and employees of the county. Except for the purpose of inquiry, the board and its members shall deal with the administrative services solely through the county manager and the heads of departments whom it may be empowered to appoint and neither the board nor any member thereof shall give orders either publicly or privately to any other county employee. Any member violating the provisions of this section shall be guilty of a misdemeanor and upon conviction thereof shall forfeit his office." Four things separate that from today's sec. 15.2-703, all of them loosening the Board: requesting an appointment is no longer barred, only dictating one; the bar on taking any part in an appointment is gone; the misdemeanor and the forfeiture of office are gone; and a sentence has been added letting the Board discuss appointments and removals with the Manager. None of that happened in 1962 (vaacts1962c623) or in 1971 (vaacts1971exsess), which leaves 1982 c. 108 or the 1997 recodification. The wording follows the National Municipal League's model (nml1916modelcharter), penalty included. What prompted the act is unknown: it is in neither the League of Women Voters' October 1951 list nor the delegation's December 1951 bill list. Filed in Drive as "legal/state statutes/Commonwealth of Virginia 1952 - Acts and Joint Resolutions, Session of 1952 (ch. 443).pdf", the page text as HathiTrust umn.31951d02280223t serves it, set out on a plain page by code/sources/pages.py and printed on 1 October 2026; HathiTrust refuses an automated request, so no copy of the page image was had.}
