      \field{annotation}{Ch. 207, Acts of the General Assembly of Virginia, session of 1958, printed pp. 263-265, approved 6 March 1958 [S 329]. The same window reopened a second time, and the last time. Sec. 15-351 is re-enacted with the single four-year-terms question that vaacts1954c151 left, and with the dates moved again - but not simply forward. The petition of "two hundred or more qualified voters" is now due by "the first day of * April nineteen hundred * fifty-eight", the court order by "the first day of * May, nineteen hundred * fifty-eight", and the poll is to be opened "at the time prescribed by law for the next * primary election to be held in * July, nineteen hundred * fifty-eight" rather than at a November general election. The asterisks are the volume's own marks on the amended words. Subsection (f) restaggers from the terms expiring in 1958, 1959, 1960 and 1961. No petition was filed, and the question has not been offered since. The chapter number is 207, not 208: 1958 c. 208 is an act about a trial judge's power to direct a verdict, printed on the same page. Filed in Drive as "legal/state statutes/Commonwealth of Virginia 1958 - Acts and Joint Resolutions, Session of 1958 (ch. 207).pdf", the page text as HathiTrust umn.31951d02280226n serves it, set out on a plain page by code/sources/pages.py and printed on 1 October 2026; HathiTrust refuses an automated request, so no copy of the page image was had.}
